  {
    "name": "MBWENI",
    "parishPriest": "Pd. Edwin Dihno",
    "location": "Mbweni",
    "contactInfo": "0784-308301",
    "imageUrl": "/img/55b0e2a7-0301-47bf-970e-827b3df91f3e_ChatGPT Image Jun 14, 2025, 12_21_36 PM.png\n",
    "email": "mbweniparish@catholicdiocese.or.tz",
    "parishPhoneNumber": "+255 784 308 301",
    "history": "Mbweni Parish, nestled along the serene coastline of Dar es Salaam, was established in the early 1980s as a response to the growing Catholic population in the Mbweni and Kunduchi areas. Initially starting as a small prayer group under a tree, the faithful gathered weekly for fellowship and spiritual nourishment.\n\nAs the community expanded, the need for a dedicated worship space became clear. Through the combined efforts of the diocese, missionaries, and local parishioners, the first church structure was constructed in 1985. Over the years, Mbweni Parish grew to include various pastoral and social ministries, including youth groups, women's empowerment programs, and outreach to the poor.\n\nToday, Mbweni Parish stands as a vibrant spiritual center, guided by its commitment to community service, evangelization, and nurturing strong Christian values among families. Its legacy continues to inspire future generations through faith, unity, and development.",
